WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:08.400
Now, I would like you to understand a fundamental concept in the database in order to understand the

00:08.400 --> 00:11.880
views, the three level architecture of the database.

00:11.880 --> 00:17.960
This architecture can describe the different levels of data abstractions in a database.

00:17.960 --> 00:19.240
So let's see what this means.

00:19.240 --> 00:22.080
So the architecture is divided into three levels.

00:22.080 --> 00:24.440
The first level is the physical level.

00:24.440 --> 00:26.400
Then we have the logical level.

00:26.400 --> 00:28.680
And the third one is the view level.

00:28.720 --> 00:30.960
Now let's understand each level what it means.

00:30.960 --> 00:32.240
So now the physical level.

00:32.400 --> 00:38.360
It is the lowest level of the database where the actual data is stored in a physical storage.

00:38.400 --> 00:44.360
And usually who has access to this layer are the database administrators, because they are the experts.

00:44.360 --> 00:49.960
And they have to manage the access and the security of this layer, because they are the experts that

00:49.960 --> 00:55.400
have to manage a lot of stuff like optimizing the performance, making sure that everything is secure,

00:55.440 --> 01:00.880
and managing the backup and recovery, and to do all the configurations and many other tasks.

01:00.880 --> 01:07.000
So at the physical layer, we have to deal with a lot of stuff like the data files, partitions, logs,

01:07.040 --> 01:13.810
catalogs, blocks and caches and many other stuff that each database needs in order to store your data.

01:13.810 --> 01:20.130
So as you can see, this layer is very complicated and you need to be really an expert of databases

01:20.130 --> 01:23.090
in order to be able to manage all those stuff.

01:23.090 --> 01:27.890
So we call this layer a physical layer, or sometimes we call it an internal layer.

01:27.890 --> 01:29.610
So now let's move to the next level.

01:29.610 --> 01:31.290
We have the logical level.

01:31.290 --> 01:34.770
So the logical layer it is less complicated than the physical layer.

01:34.810 --> 01:38.610
Here at this level you have to deal on how to organize your data.

01:38.610 --> 01:44.930
And normally we have here like an application developer or we have like data engineers that access the

01:44.930 --> 01:48.890
logical level in order to define the structure of your data.

01:48.890 --> 01:54.770
So those developers can focus on how to structure your data, rather than how the data is exactly storing

01:54.770 --> 01:56.610
the data physically at the storage.

01:56.610 --> 01:59.210
So they don't have to deal with all those details.

01:59.210 --> 02:04.450
They leave it for the database administrator, and they can focus only on how to structure the data.

02:04.730 --> 02:11.530
That's why we need for this kind of role an abstraction level for them, which is the logical level.

02:11.530 --> 02:14.690
So now what actually the developers are doing at this level?

02:14.690 --> 02:20.450
Well, they are like creating tables and defining their relationships between those tables.

02:20.450 --> 02:22.730
Or they can go and define views.

02:22.730 --> 02:27.660
They can create indexes on the tables in order to optimize the performance of the tables.

02:27.660 --> 02:33.860
Or maybe they are creating stored procedures and functions and some other codes in order to manage those

02:33.860 --> 02:34.380
tables.

02:34.420 --> 02:37.060
So as you can see, they are building the data model.

02:37.060 --> 02:40.580
They are structuring your data, but they don't care at all.

02:40.820 --> 02:44.100
Where are those data stored physically in the database.

02:44.100 --> 02:47.740
So as you can see here, things are less complicated than the physical layer.

02:47.740 --> 02:51.420
And it is a perfect abstraction for developers to build projects.

02:51.420 --> 02:56.460
So we call this the logical layer or sometimes we call it the conceptual layer.

02:56.500 --> 02:56.820
Okay.

02:56.860 --> 02:59.780
So now moving on to another level of abstraction.

02:59.780 --> 03:01.580
We have the view level.

03:01.580 --> 03:06.420
So the view level is the highest level of abstraction in the database.

03:06.420 --> 03:11.300
And it is what the end users and applications can access and can see.

03:11.300 --> 03:15.420
So for example you could have like one view for business analysts.

03:15.420 --> 03:21.260
So you prepare and customize views that are suitable only for their business analysts.

03:21.260 --> 03:22.500
And you might say you know what.

03:22.540 --> 03:29.180
Let's prepare another set of views that are suitable for data visualizations and reporting.

03:29.180 --> 03:34.900
Like you can go and connect, for example, a power BI in order to create dashboards so they are fully

03:35.070 --> 03:36.470
customized and prepared.

03:36.470 --> 03:37.030
Views.

03:37.270 --> 03:44.110
In order to be connected with the power BI reports, and you can keep doing that by creating multiple

03:44.150 --> 03:48.150
set of views that are suitable for specific purpose and use.

03:48.150 --> 03:48.670
Case.

03:48.670 --> 03:54.910
So as you can see at this level, we are exposing our data for multiple users and multiple applications.

03:54.910 --> 03:58.070
So now the question is what do we have to deal at the view level.

03:58.070 --> 04:04.750
Well you have there only views that holds only the relevant informations for the use case or users.

04:04.750 --> 04:07.550
So the users at this level have only views.

04:07.550 --> 04:13.790
They don't have to deal with the tables, indexes, stored procedures, any files, logs, partitions

04:13.790 --> 04:14.710
or anything.

04:14.710 --> 04:20.590
This is the highest level of abstraction because the focus of this layer is to make it friendly for

04:20.590 --> 04:23.070
the end users and easy to consume.

04:23.070 --> 04:28.110
So we call this layer the view layer, or sometimes we call it an external layer.

04:28.150 --> 04:33.910
So this is the three level architecture of the databases or we call it the three abstraction levels

04:33.910 --> 04:34.990
of the database.

04:34.990 --> 04:41.270
So the physical layer has the highest complexity, the lowest abstraction and the view layer has the

04:41.270 --> 04:42.510
highest abstraction.

04:42.510 --> 04:47.550
So this is one more reason why the views are very important concept in SQL databases.
